<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's KFA buys 50,000T of Brazilian soymeal.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's KFA buys 50,000T of Brazilian soymeal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Korea Feed Association (KFA) bought on late Wednesday 50,000 tonnes of Brazilian soybean meal at $309 a tonne C&amp;F from Nidera through private negotiation, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>They said shipment was set for April 1-30 to the three South Korean ports of Inchon, Kunsan and Ulsan.</p>
<p>They said premiums for ship rotation between the two ports were set at $1.5 per tonne.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
